            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "I read the three call sites. Here is the plan."
            },
            {
              "type": "tool_use",
              "id": "toolu_plan1",
              "name": "ExitPlanMode",
              "input": {
                "plan": "# Move order rounding into a shared money helper\n\nRounding lives in three places today. This plan moves it behind one helper so totals agree everywhere.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Add `roundMoney(amount, currency)` to `src/money.ts`, using banker's rounding for AUD and JPY.\n2. Replace the inline `Math.round` calls in `src/orders/totals.ts` and `src/orders/fees.ts`.\n3. Add table-driven tests in `src/money.test.ts` for half-cent and zero-decimal cases.\n4. Run the orders test suite and compare totals on the fixture orders.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Totals can shift by one cent on orders priced at exactly half a cent.\n- Fee rows are stored rounded, so existing rows are not recalculated.\n\n```ts\nexport function roundMoney(amount: number, currency: string): number {\n  const digits = currency === \"JPY\" ? 0 : 2;\n  return bankersRound(amount, digits);\n}\n```"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
